# SQL Injection Lab 2: Login Bypass

## What the Lab Asked
Login to the admin account without knowing the password.

## What I Discovered
The login form takes username and password and checks them in the database.
If both match, you login. If not, you fail.

## My Attack
I entered: administrator'--
Left password blank.

## Why It Worked
The single quote (') broke the original SQL query.
The double dash (--) commented out the password check.
So the database only verified the username, ignored the password.

## Result
Successfully logged in as admin without the password!

## What I Learned
Never trust user input directly in SQL queries.
Always validate and sanitize input.
Use prepared statements instead.
